.TH SHINY-CHAINSAW 1 "2026-10-23" "Shiny Chainsaw 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shiny-chainsaw \- lightweight Markdown viewer for technical docs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shiny-chainsaw
.RB [ -f | --file ]
.IR file
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shiny Chainsaw renders a Markdown file in a GTK3 window. Parsing is done by a
CommonMark parser implemented in the program itself; the GFM extensions (tables,
task lists, strikethrough, autolinks and the raw-HTML filter) are enabled. Images
are fetched over the network with libsoup3 or read from disk, and the open file is
re-rendered whenever it changes on disk.
.PP
With no argument a file picker is shown.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -f, --file \fIfile\fR
Open
.IR file
on startup. A file given without the flag works the same way.
.SH SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Open a file.
.TP
.B Ctrl+F
Search the document.
.TP
.B F9
Toggle the heading outline sidebar.
.TP
.B Ctrl+=, Ctrl++, Ctrl+\-, Ctrl+0
Zoom in, zoom in, zoom out, reset zoom.
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Reload the open file.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/shiny-chainsaw/recent.txt
The ten most recently opened files, most recent first.
.SH SETTINGS
The
.B image-max-width
key (GSettings schema
.BR io.github.Fate1099.shiny-chainsaw )
caps the width of rendered images in pixels. The default, 0, fits images to the
window width without upscaling them. The schema is only read once it is installed
system-wide, so running the program from a build directory falls back to 0.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR markdown (7)
